SUMMARY:Build an Agent Day - Charlotte
DESCRIPTION:All Things AI (Live)\nJoin us in [Charlotte for Build an Agent
  Day](https://www.buildanagent.io/events/charlotte-nc) and craft your own 
 AI agent live and in person! One day. One working AI agent\, built by you.
 \n\n## [Build an Agent Day - Charlotte](https://www.buildanagent.io/events
 /charlotte-nc)\n\n**Walk in with a workflow you hate. Walk out with an age
 nt that does it for you.**\n\nBuild An Agent Day is a one-day\, hands-on w
 orkshop where you codify a real task from your job as a working AI agent 
 — and leave with the design pattern to do it again and again. No slide d
 ecks to take home. By 6 PM you have something running against your own Goo
 gle Workspace or Microsoft 365 account.\nIt's a program of [All Things AI]
 (https://allthingsai.org/ "https://allthingsai.org") and [All Things Open]
 (https://allthingsopen.org/ "https://allthingsopen.org")\, built for the p
 eople who do the work: business professionals\, government leaders\, and K
 -12 and higher-ed educators. If you can write a clear how-to email\, you c
 an build an agent here.\n\n#### What you'll build\n\nOver eight hours\, yo
 u'll build the same workflow across three agent stacks and pick the one th
 at fits your environment:\n\n* **Claude Cowork** (Anthropic) — for knowl
 edge workers\n* **ChatGPT Agents** (OpenAI) — for enterprise IT\n* **Man
 us** — for research-heavy roles\n\nThe arc: pick a workflow you own (rep
 orts\, intake\, scheduling\, drafting\, research)\, capture your expertise
  as a skill an AI can follow\, wire it into your stack\, and ship it the s
 ame day. You'll demo it before you leave.\n\n#### A sample of the day\n\n*
  **Crack Open the Agent** — the three primitives (model\, tools\, memory
 ) and the agent loop\, narrated tool call by tool call\n* **Pick Your Firs
 t Three Agents** — Mark's S.M.A.R.T. framework to sort your tasks by AI 
 readiness and match each to AI\, Human\, or Both\n* **Write Your First Ski
 ll** — the anatomy of a SKILL.md\, plus worked examples including an "an
 ti-slop" quality skill and a composed website-audit skill\n* **Ship an Aut
 onomous Research Agent** — build a Morning Brief in Manus that triages e
 mail\, preps your calendar\, and ranks the day's industry news\n* **Workin
 g lunch\, three stacks\, three tables** — poke at all three with food in
  front of you\n\nThe full eight-hour arc runs at every city stop. Because 
 every workshop is live\, the schedule flexes to the room.\n\n#### Who's te
 aching\n\n**Mark Hinkle** — Workshop instructor. Founder of The AIE Netw
 ork (250\,000+ subscribers)\, co-founder of All Things AI\, 30+ years in e
 merging tech across cloud.com\, the Linux Foundation\, and the Node.js Fou
 ndation. An operator\, not a consultant.\n**Todd Lewis** — Co-founder\, 
 All Things Open. More than a decade running technology events in the Carol
 inas (POSCON\, Open Source 101\, All Things Open).\n\n#### What's included
 \n\n* Eight hours of hands-on building\n* All three agent stacks\n* Meals 
 and materials\n* The working agent you walk out with\n* A year of communit
 y access across All Things Open\, All Things AI\, and The AIE Network — 
 meetups\, virtual events\, and ongoing learning\n\n#### Pricing\n\n* **Ear
 ly bird: $297** (first 100 registrants)\n* **Standard: $397**\n\nAll tiers
  are all-inclusive. Most employers reimburse the ticket under professional
  development or continuing education budgets — receipts formatted for ex
 pense reports available on request.
